tps://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T09:00:35-07:00","id":1195318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195300#post1195300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do I have to pledge on baker kit to get the preview? allready pledged on kickstarter!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Backerkit is how you manage your kickstarter pledge and get your rewards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T09:11:11-07:00","id":1195324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195300#post1195300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do I have to pledge on baker kit to get the preview? allready pledged on kickstarter!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. You should've already completed your Scion Backerkit survey and got a Backerkit page.<br /> <br /> Go to the Backerkit page, and click on Digital Downloads. You can download the Hero preview from there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T09:38:10-07:00","id":1195330,"title":"","content":"Can I just say that I'm really impressed by the &quot;Mythic Storytelling&quot; section? It's great to see an in-depth discussion of narrative structure that isn't just paraphrased Joseph Campbell. The advice on non-western narrative structures and respectful portrayal of other cultures are also really helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:05:54-07:00","id":1195349,"title":"","content":"Okay, I am officially in love with the new Purview system! This is EVERYTHING I ever wanted out of a system to represent divine powers. <br /> <br /> Love the Marvels and all the helpful suggestions on how to use them. Love the fact that even Hero-level Boons can be straight-up &quot;Eff You&quot; buttons against one's enemies. Definitely agree with ElanConnor about that lung cancer Boon! I can't wait to go all Oregon Trail on somebody!<br /> <br /> &quot;You have died of dysentery! Or you're about to anyway!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:07:24-07:00","id":1195351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195330#post1195330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I just say that I'm really impressed by the &quot;Mythic Storytelling&quot; section? It's great to see an in-depth discussion of narrative structure that isn't just paraphrased Joseph Campbell. The advice on non-western narrative structures and respectful portrayal of other cultures are also really helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me happy to hear. I honestly didn't think that anyone would have a word to say about it this early, since there's nothing especially crunchy to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T11:28:42-07:00","id":1195391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195211#post1195211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question... Character Creation states that you get 4 dots of Callings and 2 Boons... The Traits chapter says you get 5 dots of Callings at Legend 1 and only one Boon per dot of Legend... Which is which?<br /> <br /> Also I seem to remember a post sometime ago that stated that Heroes could get 5 Boons at Legend 4, so they could max out a single Purview and their PSP... Which would imply the CC version.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am similarly confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T17:26:30-07:00","id":1195539,"title":"","content":"Sorry, it's that's a symptom of converting characters from Origin.<br /> <br /> You get 5 dots of Callings at Legend 1, and one Knack &quot;slot&quot; per Calling dot per Calling (so 3 Warrior, 1 Lover, 1 Sage, for example). The Boons thing is my fuckup too, you should get a new Boon every dot of Legend, so you've got 5 Boons at Legend 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T19:04:10-07:00","id":1195575,"title":"","content":"Got a good few hits on this last time and I enjoy it! So more words pronounced from Hero and Origins:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/folder/45708887541\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/folder/45708887541\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/folder/45708887541\" target=\"_blank\"> https://app.box.com/folder/45708887541 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T20:12:58-07:00","id":1195596,"title":"","content":"This seems to have become the general thread for comments. If this is in the wrong place for this, I'll move it.<br /> <br /> I went straight up to the Kami write-up, sharpened my knives, and... it's good. I can see where almost every element came from, and so I'm sure that the things I didn't recognise are from bits of Japanese mythology I don't know (yet). I think the author(s) made a lot of good choices from among the options available in Japanese myth, including some that I think are brilliant and wish I'd thought of. (I also think some would be better done another way, but that's only to be expected.) I love the Greatest Weakness. We Japanese (wareware nihonjin) are indeed a bit prone to that.<br /> <br /> I do have a few picky comments, though.<br /> <br /> I've never heard the &quot;Shinto saying&quot; in the epigraph, although I've seen things that are similar. What's the source? (&quot;If your heart is sincere and you follow the right path, the kami will protect you even if you do not pray&quot; is a very quick and unpoetic translation of a poem by Sugawara no Michizane, who is, of course, now a major kami, although not one you included. (I like Tenjin-sama. I got married at one of his jinja.) It's a good option because it mentions both of the Virtues.)<br /> <br /> Shinbutsu-shugo is syncretistic, not synchronistic. However, I'm inclined to leave the &quot;synchronicity&quot; later in the paragraph, because the real meaning makes sense there, and &quot;syncreticity&quot; is not a nice word.<br /> <br /> In pronunciation, &quot;Tokyo&quot; is a four-syllable word; both of the vowels are long. &quot;Kyoto&quot; is only three syllables, because only the first vowel is long. I understand that you are trying to block &quot;toe-key-oh&quot; pronunciations, but I don't think this is the best way to phrase it. Also, nobody should be using &quot;shyo&quot; as a romanisation. You do see &quot;syo&quot; as well as &quot;sho&quot;, because those are both ways to type the syllable, but not the hybrid.<br /> <br /> The figure for attended Inari jinja is very suspicious. If you define &quot;attended&quot; as &quot;someone looks after it&quot;, then it is probably too low, as all the roadside shrines should be included, along with the ones in people's gardens and the grounds of other jinja. If you mean &quot;has its own Shinto priest&quot;, then it's too high, being 12,000 higher than the number of Shinto priests in Japan. A vaguer expression would probably be better: there are lots of Inari jinja, even on roadsides, in gardens, and within the grounds of other jinja.<br /> <br /> Ame-no-Uzume is much, much more common as a reading of the kami's name than Ama-no-Uzume.<br /> <br /> Takemikazuchi's write-up refers to Namazu, but the Titan section refers to Nezumo, apparently picking up the same being. I've never heard of Nezumo, and neither has Google, but I know the legend of the catfish, Namazu, so the latter may be a typo.<br /> <br /> Under Susano-O, Susano'o-no-mikoto is a better spelling. Under Hachiman, Ojin needs a macron on the O, and Yawata is more common than Yahata. I've personally never seen Otafuku or Okame used as names for Ame-no-Uzume; they are names for the Noh mask thought to be derived from her, not for her. Under Sarutahiko, the macron is on the wrong &quot;o&quot; in Dosojin. Under Ebisu, Hiruko, not Hiroku. Under Okuninushi, Onamuji needs a macron on the initial &quot;O&quot;. Under Kisshoten, &quot;Kichijoten&quot; needs a macron on the &quot;o&quot;.<br /> <br /> In Religion: Shintoism, I've never heard the (Japanese equivalent) of &quot;Born Shinto, Married Christian, Die Buddhist&quot; in Japan, although it is common as a way to characterise it from outside. That way of thinking about religious affiliation is generally alien to Japan, so I would not really expect to hear it here, either. Better to describe it as a common saying about the Japanese, because that is certainly true. Also, same section, you mean &quot;syncretistic&quot;, not &quot;synchronistic&quot;, and lighting candles at Shinto jinja is really, really unusual.<br /> <br /> The original Yata-no-Kagami is not lost; it is in the Naiku at Ise. Similarly, the original Kusanagi no Tsurugi was not lost; Yamato Takeru left it with his wife, and it is now in Atsuta Jingu. These beliefs are fundamental to the practice of those two jinja, so I'm uncomfortable with ruling them to be inaccurate, although I can see the appeal of having them be something PC Scions can go look for. On the other hand, given the religious function of those objects, they are really inappropriate things to have as the McGuffins in a quest. You could pick some items up from the Togusa no Kandakara instead; the Life-Restoring Jewel would be an obvious one.<br /> <br /> But overall, I would be happy to play this as written, which is a first for a treatment of Shinto in an RPG. Well done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10351-dchart","name":"dchart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T20:28:09-07:00","id":1195598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195539#post1195539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, it's that's a symptom of converting characters from Origin.<br /> <br /> You get 5 dots of Callings at Legend 1, and one Knack &amp;quot;slot&amp;quot; per Calling dot per Calling (so 3 Warrior, 1 Lover, 1 Sage, for example). The Boons thing is my fuckup too, you should get a new Boon every dot of Legend, so you've got 5 Boons at Legend 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any clarification on Asset Skills? I posted a fairly detailed post about two pages back in the ask neall thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T03:43:02-07:00","id":1195677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195259#post1195259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, two problems with Fatebinding:<br /> <br /> 1) Does resolution have to be so strict? The Rival sticks out because not everyone with that is tsundere for their counterpart, and many aren't even unfriendly about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing in the Rival Condition that requires the characters to be unfriendly about it, just that they want to show each other up. That can absolutely take the form of a friendly, encouraging rivalry as easily as fist-shaking fury. As for the Resolution, sure, if it makes sense you can change the Paramour result (but IMHO smoldering romantic tension is by far the most fun).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195259#post1195259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The Traitor has a hidden Role. Okay... What kind of Role? Does it have to be a negative role? If it isn't, why is it called Traitor? I don't think a Jinx who is actually a Boon Companion is someone the Scion is mad at. Grounds for sacrificing 100 cattle to whatever gods of fortune are in her pantheon, but not mad.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it looks great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't have to be. I mean, if you're going for the classic &quot;I'm going to smile at you until I stick a knife in your back,&quot; yeah, Jinx or Nemesis or what have you, but mechanically it works just fine for, say, &quot;I'm secretly in love with you&quot; or the like. Basically, if you can come up with a justification for the relationship that makes sense to your table, go for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T05:26:20-07:00","id":1195688,"title":"","content":"I just did a second read through but I can't seem to find the advice/guidelines on Denizen path creation. Could have sworn there was something in there","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T05:57:01-07:00","id":1195695,"title":"","content":"A quick question: does the possible Birthrights from Origin (One of the character creation options is that rather than extra skills you get 4 points in Birthrights) stack with the 7 Birthright points from your visitation? For a total of 11 points in Birthrights.<br /> <br /> I presume that if it is that way, it's pretty much only if you played through the &quot;Origin&quot; Stage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23677,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23677-the-eternal-keeper","user":"The Eternal Keeper","date":". 03-15-2018, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23677-the-eternal-keeper","name":"The Eternal Keeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T06:50:53-07:00","id":1195710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195539#post1195539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, it's that's a symptom of converting characters from Origin.<br /> <br /> You get 5 dots of Callings at Legend 1, and one Knack &quot;slot&quot; per Calling dot per Calling (so 3 Warrior, 1 Lover, 1 Sage, for example). The Boons thing is my fuckup too, you should get a new Boon every dot of Legend, so you've got 5 Boons at Legend 4.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> if is 1 boon for legend why 5 boon at legend 4?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T07:46:59-07:00","id":1195724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195710#post1195710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> if is 1 boon for legend why 5 boon at legend 4?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm guessing it's 2 Boons at Legend 1 - one for reaching Hero, and one for Legend 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5619-starkjunior","name":"StarkJunior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T09:27:43-07:00","id":1195754,"title":"","content":"So now chapter 2 (and chapter 3 technically) are read.<br /> <br /> First impression. Wow. The amount and depth of research that obviously went into each pantheon is staggering. I know some people will disagree with the interpretations that the scion team chose but no one can deny that each interpretation is an informed and researched choice.<br /> Again, i wish to present my respect to the scion team for the in-depth research they've done. <br /> <br /> A minor ... its not even a nitpick. Its just that i really like the sections about relationship with other pantheons and i'd like to read more of that. I get limits on word count and the like. But its something that i'd like to see developed more. <br /> <br /> A curiosity. I dont remember any mention of Izanagi and Izanami in the Kami section. Nor is there any indication of a primordial for the Kami. Is is slated for a future book (like the demigod of god one maybe)?<br /> <br /> Now starting chapter 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T10:40:15-07:00","id":1195784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195754#post1195754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A curiosity. I dont remember any mention of Izanagi and Izanami in the Kami section. Nor is there any indication of a primordial for the Kami. Is is slated for a future book (like the demigod of god one maybe)?</div> </div> </div> </div>They both get a couple of mentions in individual Kami's writeups. The most relevant two are Amaterasu and Susano-O's.<br /> <br /> &quot;Amaterasu was the firstborn of the three Kami born from the Primordial Izanagi and Izanami, who declared her ruler of all.&quot; (p. 80)<br /> <br /> &quot;He [Susano-O] cried for his mother, Izanami, demanding to see her, even though she had died and traveled to Yomi.&quot; (p. 81)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T10:58:42-07:00","id":1195789,"title":"","content":"So, a thing I adore? 2e's Fatebinding. You can USE this. The Storyguide can use them. The Fatebindings can <i>shift </i>and <i>change</i>.<br /> <br /> It's possible for my Tuatha Scion to save a plucky mortal one night while Freelance Heroing, and Fatebind them as a Balm to sooth his flaring emotions (though mostly fluffed as the Fatebonded using snark to take the wind out of his sails).<br /> <br /> Then after a particularly flashy and serious display of Prowess, the Fatebonded can realize the true gravity of being a Scion... And changes to Boon Companion, providing more regular help and backup.<br /> <br /> Then after a moment where the Fatebonded helps save the day, possibly by driving a car into an enemy that was threatening the Scion, the two are standing there in the aftermath... And then have sloppy make-outs. Boom. Boon Companion to Paramour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T12:19:29-07:00","id":1195813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195784#post1195784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They both get a couple of mentions in individual Kami's writeups. The most relevant two are Amaterasu and Susano-O's.<br /> <br /> &quot;Amaterasu was the firstborn of the three Kami born from the Primordial Izanagi and Izanami, who declared her ruler of all.&quot; (p. 80)<br /> <br /> &quot;He [Susano-O] cried for his mother, Izanami, demanding to see her, even though she had died and traveled to Yomi.&quot; (p. 81)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah thanks. I read the whole chapter basically in one go and i completely forgot those parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T14:22:41-07:00","id":1195845,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">My deity wishlist for the Companion to bring every Pantheon up to 17 major players...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Aesir: Bragi, Idunn, Ullr, and Vidar</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Deva: Ganga, Chandra, and Brahma (yes I know he's currently a Primordial, but he was more active in the World as a God in the past, so i think it would have value to write-him-up as reflected in those traditions for those who want to use him that way)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Kami: Oyamatsumi and Konohanasakuya-hime</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Manitou/Orenda: Kitchi-Odjig, Hawenneyu, Doyadastethe, Akonwara, Doendzowes, Aireskoi, Hinon</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Netjer: Neber-Het, Bes, Neith, Serquet, and Renenutet</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Orisha: Oba and Aganju</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Shen: Yao, Shun, Yu, and Xiwangmu (as with Brahma)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Teotl: Tlazolteotl, Camaxtli, Mayahuel, and Xolotl</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Theoi: Hecate and Pan</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">(and I'm still working on the Tuatha - all I currently have for them is Cailleach, which still leaves me with three more to choose)</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Obviously there are more that would be cool for many of these Pantheons beyond these! But these strike me as the highest priority if you set the easiest target to even out the numbers.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-16-2018, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T15:13:11-07:00","id":1195864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195845#post1195845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serquet</div> </div> </div> </div>The Homestuck jokes would never end!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T15:21:53-07:00","id":1195867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195864#post1195864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Homestuck jokes would never end!</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to read that one day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T18:03:26-07:00","id":1195913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Aesir: Bragi, Idunn, Ullr, and Vidar</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Someone's been watching The Almighty Johnsons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T18:28:05-07:00","id":1195917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195913#post1195913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Someone's been watching The Almighty Johnsons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, those are just the most prominent Aesir who aren't in the current set. Never seen the show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T05:08:13-07:00","id":1196013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195845#post1195845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">My deity wishlist for the Companion to bring every Pantheon up to 17 major players...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Kami: Oyamatsumi and Konohanasakuya-hime</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't go for them. Tenjin, because he is one of the Big Four kami, and a good example of a mortal who advanced to godhood. Not sure about the other; I'd need to spend longer thinking about what is missing from the current line-up. (I would make Izanagi and Izanami more Titan than Primordial, because they spend a lot of time on the World and Izanami is locked away underground because she threatens to kill everyone. Takamimusubi and Kamimusubi are Primordials, though: they arise first in the World, and then hide themselves away. They both send aspects into the Overworld from time to time, but never (AFAIR) manifest in the World.)<br /> <br /> The other three of the Big Four are Amaterasu, Hachiman, and Inari, so they are already in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10351-dchart","name":"dchart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T08:54:34-07:00","id":1196081,"title":"","content":"Thanks dchart! I hadn\u2019t realized Tenjin\u2019s religious prominence. I\u2019ll move him up my list and the other two down. Any suggestion on a goddess you\u2019d want to see with Tenjin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:15:56-07:00","id":1196157,"title":"","content":"So one thing I noticed reading through Hero and it was kinda there in the previews of the pantheon as well that people were discussing it.<br /> <br /> The Orisha still have their descriptive sentence where apparently they compare anyone who considers Titans, y'know, <i>Titans</i> to the Nazis. Which is kind of offputting about them in general. Like, them thinking Titan is a political term is fine and valid, but them basically equating anyone who doesn't agree with them with a phrase commenting on people who kept to their own business while innocents were rounded up by Nazi Germany is a <i>stupendously</i> gauche way of putting it, especially when those &quot;innocents&quot; in that metaphor include Surtr and Apep/Apophis.<br /> <br /> Similarly, their primary weakness comes up as a little shaky to me. &quot;Systemic racism and religious intolerance&quot;. Basically every other Pantheon has a weakness that's internal to the Pantheon. The Aesir are semi-mortal and capable of aging and dying. The Tuatha make their own dooms in their geasa that enemies can exploit. The Netjer and the Theoi have massive in-fighting problems, and the Shen have so many of themselves that organization is almost impossible. The Kami have the greatest egos about themselves there ever was. The Manitou are trying to reinvent themselves to appeal to modern followers without losing the traditions that make them who they are.<br /> <br /> The closest thing to the Orisha in terms of weakness is the Deva, who are basically the biggest target for Titan attacks due to the size of their religion and their arsenal, and even <i>that</i> has an element of internality in that the Deva response to people seeing them as threatening is to go &quot;Well you wanna make a big deal? Come at me bro!&quot;<br /> <br /> The Orisha, by comparison, have a weakness that basically spells out &quot;man, the world would be great if it weren't for all you other people&quot;, which seems... disingenuous?<br /> <br /> Like, their Titan stance could be a weakness in and of itself, since it's something internal to them that causes problems from both the outside (tension with Pantheons that have titanomachy issues) and inside (the fact that holding to this stance kind of blinds them to the threat posed by actual Titans that live down to the stereotypes of titanomachy that all the other pantheons accept). It becomes more of a double edged sword issue that IS an issue, like the Tuatha geasa, as opposed to basically spelling out their weakness as &quot;everyone else is assholes to us, woe is us&quot;. I suppose it may be <i>historically</i> correct in that is their greatest weakness, but I have trouble keeping my suspension of disbelief in place that the Orisha get the primary religious intolerance when what wordcount is spent on the subject of Abrahamic religions kind of glosses over all the other polytheistic religions that might experience religious intolerance for the same reasons, yet none of them are even mentioned, especially in a World where all of the above are true and at least marginally accepted as such.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the rambling, but that section just still strikes me as off-key compared to how well the rest of the books handles these things, and in fact how good the rest of the Orisha section is for a pantheon I'm not personally super-familiar with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:19:58-07:00","id":1196159,"title":"","content":"For the Tuatha, maybe <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elcmar\" target=\"_blank\">Elcmar</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuireann\" target=\"_blank\">Tuireann</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aed_(god)\" target=\"_blank\">Aed/Aodh</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flidais\" target=\"_blank\">Flidais</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuamnach\" target=\"_blank\">Fuamnach</a>. All kind of obscure, though.<br /> <br /> e: or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cailleach\" target=\"_blank\">Cailleach</a>, though I'm unclear on if she's one person or a type of creature or both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:28:12-07:00","id":1196162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OpMegs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196157#post1196157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, their Titan stance could be a weakness in and of itself, since it's something internal to them that causes problems from both the outside (tension with Pantheons that have titanomachy issues) and inside (the fact that holding to this stance kind of blinds them to the threat posed by actual Titans that live down to the stereotypes of titanomachy that all the other pantheons accept). It becomes more of a double edged sword issue that IS an issue, like the Tuatha geasa, as opposed to basically spelling out their weakness as &quot;everyone else is assholes to us, woe is us&quot;. I suppose it may be <i>historically</i> correct in that is their greatest weakness, but I have trouble keeping my suspension of disbelief in place that the Orisha get the primary religious intolerance when what wordcount is spent on the subject of Abrahamic religions kind of glosses over all the other polytheistic religions that might experience religious intolerance for the same reasons, yet none of them are even mentioned, especially in a World where all of the above are true and at least marginally accepted as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, if you want to talk about the systemic impact of the weakness, you just need to change the framing. For example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Orisha's greatest weakness is that they are a people shattered. The slave trade that so hurt their worshipers also impacted them profoundly. Even now, years later, they often try to recover who they are, and who they were. They're torn now, even between their identities as the Orisha and the Loa, pulled in two directions by two different people who need them. </div> </div> </div>You know, just spitballing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:28:46-07:00","id":1196163,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I hate to play this card but I am personally as kind of annoyed that the Orisha's weakness is that even as gods they are victimized and marginalized along with their worshipers even in Scion 2nd Edition's seemingly more inclusive world. Paying mention to the Atlantic Slave Trade and how it created a syncretic religion is both important and necessary but I think it goes to far into somewhat defining the Orisha by their oppression. Something all the other pantheons don't seem to have to deal with. <br /> <br /> But, hey, I could see how this more &quot;relevant&quot; depiction is attractive for some people so I won't complain to much, but I will say that last few years have kind of drained me when it moves to &quot;Black Struggle Media&quot; which seems to be one of the only forms of representation and stories we get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:33:46-07:00","id":1196167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorsRattus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196159#post1196159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">e: or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cailleach\" target=\"_blank\">Cailleach</a>, though I'm unclear on if she's one person or a type of creature or both.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's Scottish, not one of the Tuatha or related to them sadly. She is a folkloric figure who has no evidence of worship, veneration, or the like. Early 20th century scholars suggested she was an Irish Goddess (you can see the publication in <i>Folklore</i> from 1927 at the bottom) but that has been subsequently abandoned since it was based in a misunderstanding, and a <i>lot</i> of assumptions. But, modern pop-culture hasn't caught up to that, and tends to depict her as an Irish Goddess. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, she isn't a Goddess, or Irish. She's a folkloric Scottish winter personification. She's about as much one of the Tuatha as the Grim Reaper is. The confusion behind it all is in her name, as several Irish figures share similar ones. (The word is based on an Irish word for Nun or Old Woman, so, the names are popular) <br /> <br /> The Tuatha are a pain because the majority of their figures are so minimally depicted with only names being given to us, that statting them out is really tricky. Fand is probably possible, I did an example of Midir on the forums when someone wanted a member of the Tuatha who had Hunter, Bobd Derg might work as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:52:03-07:00","id":1196183,"title":"","content":"active worship is not a requirement for Godhood in Scion. There\u2019s no evidence Loki ever received worship, and Baba Yaga definitely didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> A Gaelic personification of Winter I think is completely appropriate example of someone who originated from the Tuatha but rose to her Godhood well after the recorded epics of pagan Ireland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T13:09:54-07:00","id":1196189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196167#post1196167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The word is based on an Irish word for Nun or Old Woman, so, the names are popular</div> </div> </div> </div>Roughly speaking Seanbhean would be old woman, where as Cailleach sort of means a &quot;really&quot; old woman, with connotations of an elderly widowed/unmarried woman who lives alone or a really old matriarch or a witch, or also an insult. English &quot;hag&quot; is quite close in having most of the same meanings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T13:24:00-07:00","id":1196199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196183#post1196183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">active worship is not a requirement for Godhood in Scion. There\u2019s no evidence Loki ever received worship, and Baba Yaga definitely didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> A Gaelic personification of Winter I think is completely appropriate example of someone who originated from the Tuatha but rose to her Godhood well after the recorded epics of pagan Ireland.</div> </div> </div> </div>Active worship isn't a necessity at all, we have no record of any of the Tuatha being worshiped. But, it's a good flag when we are uncertain. I wouldn't be comfortable making her a Goddess when the people who believed in her didn't think she was one, and would probably be <i>very</i> uncomfortable with the idea of it, feels like it's stealing and reshaping a traditional belief. I also don't use Baba Yaga as a Goddess either. But, to each their own, people can do whatever they'd like in their own games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T16:03:09-07:00","id":1196262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196081#post1196081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks dchart! I hadn\u2019t realized Tenjin\u2019s religious prominence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Shinto actually is a living, continuous tradition in the real world, the prominence of kami is not very closely related to their prominence in the myths. Tenjin, of course, was born over a hundred years after the myths were written down. (The main difference between Japan in the real world and Japan in the World seems to be that the World has more talking foxes.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196081#post1196081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll move him up my list and the other two down. Any suggestion on a goddess you\u2019d want to see with Tenjin?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we need a female kami, Shirayama-hime/Kukuri-hime (same kami, different names). One mention in one version of one myth in the Nihonshoki, but lots of jinja. Konohanasakuya-hime is actually a possibility; not as widespread as Shirayama-hime, but she's a kami of cherry blossoms, childbirth, and volcanoes. It's an interesting combination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10351-dchart","name":"dchart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T20:00:18-07:00","id":1196333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dchart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196262#post1196262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Konohanasakuya-hime is actually a possibility; not as widespread as Shirayama-hime, but she's a kami of cherry blossoms, childbirth, and volcanoes. It's an interesting combination.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, she's definitely still on my list, I'd just want to include her together with her dad. I find his identity as one of the born children of Izanami and Izanagi, predating the three children created by Izanagi purifying after seeing Izanami in the Underworld, a potentially fascinating source for tension in the Amatsukami v Kunitsukami political tension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T20:58:09-07:00","id":1196354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dchart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196262#post1196262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we need a female kami, Shirayama-hime/Kukuri-hime (same kami, different names). One mention in one version of one myth in the Nihonshoki, but lots of jinja.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you characterize how she's seen? I can find very little information besides her widespread worship and the one mention Nihongi, which appears to have lost context (Izanagi praises her words, but said words are not included).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T21:13:37-07:00","id":1196356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196354#post1196354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would you characterize how she's seen? I can find very little information besides her widespread worship and the one mention Nihongi, which appears to have lost context (Izanagi praises her words, but said words are not included).</div> </div> </div> </div>She's seen as a go-between between Izanagi and Izanami at that point, at the border with the Underworld. The Shirayama cult is one of the sacred mountain cults, which means that a lot was lost in the Meiji period, so I would need to dig a bit. Shirayamahime Jinja also enshrines Izanagi and Izanami, which makes things more complex.<br /> <br /> A good one with more written records would be Okinagatarashi-hime, who is one third of the Hachiman kami, and would have the Guardian, Judge, and Warrior callings. If all the myths are true in the World, she conquered the Korean peninsula in the third century, while pregnant. The problem with her is that Hachiman=Ojin is already written in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10351-dchart","name":"dchart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T21:34:43-07:00","id":1196359,"title":"","content":"So Shirayama could serve as a liminal figure between the chthonic and the ouranic? Like give her Death, Journeys, and Sky?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T23:48:23-07:00","id":1196391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195845#post1195845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Aesir: Bragi, Idunn, Ullr, and Vidar</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can see this, but I can't help wondering if Hodr should get in before Bragi<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Deva: Ganga, Chandra, and Brahma (yes I know he's currently a Primordial, but he was more active in the World as a God in the past, so i think it would have value to write-him-up as reflected in those traditions for those who want to use him that way)</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Well, good news is that Brahma has Callings and Purviews in the Origin appendix, so I'm assuming he'll be in the core book. The other two seem the best inclusions<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Kami: Oyamatsumi and Konohanasakuya-hime</span></span> </div> </div> </div>This has been covered extensively, and I don't have much to add except that I'm still not convinced that Ryujin is Ao Guang.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Manitou/Orenda: Kitchi-Odjig, Hawenneyu, Doyadastethe, Akonwara, Doendzowes, Aireskoi, Hinon</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I... I really don't like that Anishinaabaek and Haudenosaunee myth has been conflated like this. I really don't. But since that's what we have here, this list is about as good as could be expected, save that I perhaps would have Onatah in place of her father, as I haven't seen much in the way of actual myths for the latter (though even then, I'd see them both over Tawiscara, who I really think should be a Titan)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Netjer: Neber-Het, Bes, Neith, Serquet, and Renenutet</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Neber-het, Bes, and probably Neith and Serqet seem fine, but I've always had a soft spot for Anhur. I could even see Kebauet if they want to really cover what was possible in 1e, or Bastet (who is explicitly not Bast here, and was rather important in her own right).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Orisha: Oba and Aganju</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I really think Erinle is an obvious choice for the Orisha, very popular and with an interesting water/earth duality. I've seen some takes where there's a gender difference there, but I'm not able to find anything reliable right now on that front. Either way, I think they'd be a more interesting choice than Oba.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Shen: Yao, Shun, Yu, and Xiwangmu (as with Brahma)</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, one short here. Also, more good news, Xiwangmu also has stuff already set out in Origins. Otherwise, I can't really agree with this. I understand wanting more of the Five Emperors present, but I think there are too many more varied, interesting, and/or popular deities in the pantheon that could be included, like Caishen, Wenchang Wang, Mazu, and Houyi (which the full Hero text confirms is totally someone who you could be a Scion of).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Teotl: Tlazolteotl, Camaxtli, Mayahuel, and Xolotl</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I really think Xiuhtecuhtli is someone who should be in here. Tlazolteotl and Mixcoatl are too important to leave out, I think, and while I think Xolotl is more prominent than Mayahuel, that puts a really big gender gap there. Hmmm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Theoi: Hecate and Pan</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I just don't buy Pan. He's prominent, yes, but he dies, and that's just not something the Theoi can do. I don't think he topped Legend 8. My vote would be for Tyche, whose cult was surprisingly widespread all things considered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">(and I'm still working on the Tuatha - all I currently have for them is Cailleach, which still leaves me with three more to choose)</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Tuatha are hard. I love Watcher's Midir, and Fand is probably workable, but even after that the best I can think of would be the likes of Bobd Derg, Cian, or Niamh, and those aren't particularly strong choices all things considered.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12989,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","user":"Center-of-All","date":". 03-17-2018, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T00:04:52-07:00","id":1196393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196391#post1196391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I just don't buy Pan. He's prominent, yes, but he dies, and that's just not something the Theoi can do. I don't think he topped Legend 8. My vote would be for Tyche, whose cult was surprisingly widespread all things considered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... death and rebirth is something Dionysus has done too, at least according to his own Mysteries. And that's making the huge leap to assume Plutarch got the details right about Pan, when it's perfectly plausible that what was actually heard over the water was &quot;Thamus Panmegas tethneke&quot; (All-Great Tammuz is dead! - a perfectly reasonable thing to hear about a dying and resurrecting god like Tammuz) and not &quot;Thamous Pan ho megas techneke&quot; (&quot;Thamus, Great Pan is dead!&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T00:32:46-07:00","id":1196401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196391#post1196391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I really don't like that Anishinaabaek and Haudenosaunee myth has been conflated like this. I really don't. But since that's what we have here, this list is about as good as could be expected, save that I perhaps would have Onatah in place of her father, as I haven't seen much in the way of actual myths for the latter (though even then, I'd see them both over Tawiscara, who I really think should be a Titan)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, wanting to flesh out the Orenda beyond the two-brothers is in large part based on the desire to see them presented as a distinct Pantheon in identity, even if a metaphysically and ancestrally overlapping one (thanks to [Sky-Woman] in their mythic roots); and not some secondary Manitou off-shoot.<br /> <br /> I don't see why the brother of a god who is in a dualistic relationship with him would be a Titan. What I know about Flint paint him as very human in his selfishness and spite, and not with the &quot;othering&quot; elements we see with most of the beings labeled as Titans in the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T11:06:37-07:00","id":1196538,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't see much of a consistent &quot;Othering&quot; theme with the Titans. Yes, Tawiscara is selfish and spiteful like humans, in the same sense that Cronus is paranoid and jealous like humans, or that Bres is a hot asshole who just wants to keep his job despite sucking at it. Frankly, most of the actual greek Titans don't seem particularly distinguishable from the Olynpians in terms of their behaviour. I think of Tawiscara as a Titan due to the severity of his actions wrt trying to end the world via famine, and due to never really having positive interactions with the rest of his pantheon or their worshipers, at least that I could find (and no, lying to Ataentsic doesn't count), and that's the sort of thing that I look for in the absence of obvious purview monofocus or an explicit in mythology division like the greeks or hittites have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T15:50:36-07:00","id":1196629,"title":"","content":"Question: Is Artemis a virgin or a lesbian in this edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T17:15:27-07:00","id":1196646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196629#post1196629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Is Artemis a virgin or a lesbian in this edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>She's honestly probably asexual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T17:18:05-07:00","id":1196647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196538#post1196538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't see much of a consistent &quot;Othering&quot; theme with the Titans. Yes, Tawiscara is selfish and spiteful like humans, in the same sense that Cronus is paranoid and jealous like humans, or that Bres is a hot asshole who just wants to keep his job despite sucking at it. Frankly, most of the actual greek Titans don't seem particularly distinguishable from the Olynpians in terms of their behaviour. I think of Tawiscara as a Titan due to the severity of his actions wrt trying to end the world via famine, and due to never really having positive interactions with the rest of his pantheon or their worshipers, at least that I could find (and no, lying to Ataentsic doesn't count), and that's the sort of thing that I look for in the absence of obvious purview monofocus or an explicit in mythology division like the greeks or hittites have.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something I'd definitely be more interested in talking about, so please feel free to PM me. We didn't want to other Tawiscara because he's still very much focused on humanity, though he was a judgment call to include no matter what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T17:28:58-07:00","id":1196653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196646#post1196646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's honestly probably asexual.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Athena at my table. Artemis is.... Incredibly gay!<br /> (And I will throw my shoes at the first person why tries to bring up Hyginus' perversion of the Orion myth!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-17-2018, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T17:07:57-07:00","id":1196957,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10351-dchart\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10351\" data-vbnamecard=\"10351\">dchart</a> <br /> <br /> How do you imagine using Ninigi-no-Mikoto in the setting? Active deity? Cyclical god who used to Incarnate as Emperors, but hasn't been heard from since New Years '46?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T17:37:47-07:00","id":1196971,"title":"","content":"Its out for backers, has a general release date been determined?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T18:37:52-07:00","id":1196990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196971#post1196971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its out for backers, has a general release date been determined?</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn\u2019t even the formatted pdf with art where they crowd source final errata yet. Before final art and formatting is done they\u2019re not going to attach dates when there\u2019s still work that they can\u2019t know how long it will take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T19:26:20-07:00","id":1197007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196653#post1196653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's Athena at my table. Artemis is.... Incredibly gay!<br /> (And I will throw my shoes at the first person why tries to bring up Hyginus' perversion of the Orion myth!)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ooh, I could use some new shoes. What size are you?<br /> <br /> But, yeah, for my part I agree with Neall on this one. I have been under the impression that Artemis' disinterest in romance or marriage was related to her associations with childhood and her status as protector of prepubescent girls. It emphasizes her Peter Panishness, and an utter lack of sexuality is a major part of that (not that children work that way in real life, but symbolically it's a pretty big deal.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T19:42:26-07:00","id":1197011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197007#post1197007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ooh, I could use some new shoes. What size are you?<br /> <br /> But, yeah, for my part I agree with Neall on this one. I have been under the impression that Artemis' disinterest in romance or marriage was related to her associations with childhood and her status as protector of prepubescent girls. It emphasizes her Peter Panishness, and an utter lack of sexuality is a major part of that (not that children work that way in real life, but symbolically it's a pretty big deal.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hence all those male children brought into her retinue to play with the beautiful young maidens she collects?<br /> <br /> I think the Peter Pan image (as used by Rick Riordan) for her is cute, but I don't think it fits the legends where the women she selected for her retinue are all old enough to wed, never young children.<br /> <br /> She may have &quot;lacked sexuality&quot; because the male Ancient Greeks didn't conceive of sapphic sexuality as sexuality.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying with the complete absence of recorded sapphic representation among gods (thanks to the men who wrote down the legends we have access to not conceiving of sapphic sex as sex), with THREE major &quot;virgin&quot; goddesses on Olympus, I think one can budge in how we interpret said &quot;virginity&quot; in a modern context - and the one who immediately ran off to hang with nymphs and beautiful maidens after getting her dad to promise she didn't have to get married is the obvious choice.<br /> <br /> Though if someone wanted to point to the Pallas myth as beloved &quot;best-friend&quot; of Athena, instead of being a Giant she slew, to argue she's the one who should be reinterpreted in that light, that would be fair as well, though that particular legend is such an outlier with regard to her relationship with women in myth that it's not my first choice.<br /> <br /> <br /> [sidenote: none of this is the shoes throwing impetus. That's just the &quot;Artemis was actually into a dude!&quot; - because that Hyginus myth is bullshit. Orion was killed by a giant scorpion because he boasted he could slay every animal on the earth, Apollo had nothing to do with it, and other than possibly hunting with her and Leto once, there's no hint of a 'special relationship' with Artemis anywhere else]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-18-2018, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T23:37:52-07:00","id":1197057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196391#post1196391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hmmm, one short here. Also, more good news, Xiwangmu also has stuff already set out in Origins. Otherwise, I can't really agree with this. I understand wanting more of the Five Emperors present, but I think there are too many more varied, interesting, and/or popular deities in the pantheon that could be included, like Caishen, Wenchang Wang, Mazu, and Houyi (which the full Hero text confirms is totally someone who you could be a Scion of).<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Caishen was meant to be on that list too, hence being one short. Mazu would definitely work! I'm trying to imagine how Houyi works here except as an Incarnate - since his failure to achieve immortality is such an important part of his narrative.<br /> <br /> Wenchang Wang would be hard to give a distinct niche since his whole purview is currently covered by Master Kung.<br /> <br /> With the 3 emperors I included on my list I was thinking their roles as Minister of Heaven (Yao), Minister of Earth (Shun), and Minister of Water (Yu) could be played up to give them more distinct roles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T00:35:42-07:00","id":1197070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1196957#post1196957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10351-dchart\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10351\" data-vbnamecard=\"10351\">dchart</a><br /> <br /> How do you imagine using Ninigi-no-Mikoto in the setting? Active deity? Cyclical god who used to Incarnate as Emperors, but hasn't been heard from since New Years '46?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably never went above Demigod, actually died, not around any more? He's really not that important in Shinto myth and practice. Now, Jinmu Tenno was and is significant, and maybe Meiji Tenno was an Incarnation of him.<br /> <br /> I'll almost certainly do something with Japan, probably the Tokyo area as that's where I live, for the Community Content program, and I would want to cover that sort of thing there, while avoiding contradicting anything in the rules-as-written. (If any actual Shinto priests read the bit about having sex under torii in Origin, though, they will be very, very unhappy. In a &quot;don't give people ideas&quot; sort of way. Jinja do have a number of problems caused by popular superstitions, and they don't need that one adding to the list...)<br /> <br /> No comment on Purviews yet. I'm still reading and mulling, and figuring out how to make things fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10351-dchart","name":"dchart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T15:47:30-07:00","id":1197368,"title":"","content":"I'm back from a back-to-back reading of Origin and Hero, and my dominant feeling is spurned lover's disappointment and frustration: I kept getting way excited about all those excellent character-building ideas about Pantheons, Mantles, different brands of Scions and legendary creatures, Callings, Paths, Purviews, marvels, and incredibly frustrated about how the system goes out of its way to impose strict power-level and niche-preserving limits that make the game all but unplayable for my (high-powered and broad-ranging) playstyle tastes. The utter inability to buy more than an handful Boons in the very best of cases (and hence build up decent use of all but the narrowest set of Purviews, given the extreme scarcity of Legend juice to use Marvel rules) no matter the character-creation tweaks and even an exceedingly long time playing the same character (one might play a scion the time it would take to build a mage or beast to Archmage or Incarnate levels, and fail to make a noticeable bump in their abilities ), and the strict dependency on cumbersome physical tools and props to have an array of supernatural powers exceeding a single field, no matter contrary character concepts. Moreover, almost all the combat-worthy and really impressive supernatural power applications are gated behind expenditure of a resource that is very scarce and quite difficult to refuel (you can only perform sacrifice w/o making it a session-defining event once in a great while, and there obvious limits to how many Fatebindings you may accumulate w/o making it ridiculous and unmanageable), much worse than it would typically take a CotD supernatural to refill their power pool stat.<br /> <br /> I came to this game expecting I would be able to play a divinely empowered if still somewhat inexperienced high-tier comic-book or anime superhero, say Avatar Korra at the beginning of her series, then I realized I would not even be able to play the equivalent of an experienced bender, wizard, or mid-tier superhero, and the game in practice is going to keep the play nailed to the level of street-level action-adventure with a few supernatural tricks once in a great while or low-level Vancian magic-user, and no change being possible beyond the release of a book that for what I know has not yet reached first draft status. In the meanwhile, you can play a Daredevil, Punisher, or James Bond clone that can perhaps throw a lightning bolt or shapechange once every two or three game sessions or so. Not really my notion of playing the second coming of Hercules or Sun Wukong, even at the beginning of their heroic journeys. If one looks to the situation hard enough, it seems one would do much a better job of using rules for say CotD Mage or Beast, or superhumans in Mutants and Masterminds, reskinned with Scion flavor and setting, than using this &quot;look, don't touch&quot; system to play these supposedly awesome divine champions a properly developed supernatural can run circles around and wipe floors with.<br /> <br /> At the very, very least, I'd deem the game only playable with an extensive set of hacks, such as a) making the players able to buy up more Boons (and Knacks) with experience in each of their Purviews and Callings/Supenatural Paths, say up to 1-2 Boons per Purview and 2-3 per Calling, even if they only can activate a limited amount per scene b) providing a less cumbersome way for scions to refuel Legend, such as performance of dramatically-appropriate heroic deeds, or alternatively switch all Boons that aren't more powerful than fireball-throwing or changing shape from spending Legend to imbuing it c) explictly allowing use of 'nominal' Relics that cannot be effectively lost or stolen to channel Purviews for those characters whose concepts are not supposed to be reliant on physical props and tools d) make all starting characters begin at Legend 4.<br /> <br /> Or alternatively, I suppose I'd just drop Origin and Hero into a distant corner of my HD and library, and pretend hard the game doesn't exist until Demigod and God get written and released, in the hopeful expectation the system limits enforced by the game get less hardcore hostile to my playstyle tastes. And hopefully by Demigod or God at last I get to play my Avatar Korra clone with extensive mastery and easy use of say a half-dozen Purviews (or generalist jack of all trades expertise in a dozen ones) and zero dependency on tools and props without having to rewrite half the system. But at this point I'm much more dubious than when I pledged to the KS. Again, I feel weird that the setting and the flavor portion of the game provide all these incredible ideas that I can't really use in play except once in a blue moon, and then I realize I can make a much more properly impressive version of these supposedly awesome divine heroes with reskinned CotD supernatural or superhero RPG rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-19-2018, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T16:42:00-07:00","id":1197386,"title":"","content":"What a long winded way of saying that not every game meets everyone's tastes, and that this one doesn't meet yours. Origin and Hero were never intended to be &quot;high-powered and broad-ranging&quot;, nor should they be. This is the beginning of the journey, not the middle, or the end. Exalted (Solars) TC: Aberrant (When it comes out), or perhaps even Scion: Demigod (Once again, when it comes out) are more likely to be to your tastes, but please don't act like Origin and Hero don't set the stage for your basic starting level Heroic Myths, because they do, and they do it well. Jason, Paris, Orion, Cassandra, Theseus, Cadmus, Achilles, Odysseus, Orpheus, Hector, Ajax, Perseus, even Heracles once you get a few more points of legend under your belt, are all possible with Scion: Hero, and that's just a fraction of the heroes, and only the Theoi.<br /> <br /> Points of Legend aren't often spent except for Big Effects, and Miracles, and getting Legend back isn't that hard since gaining, or compelling, a fate binding are things that refresh it, and you can make a minor sacrifice to get a point of Legend back once per session with simply a neat description of what you did. Most boons simply require you to imbue it into the effect, and you can retrieve it when ever you wish by simply deactivating what ever it was that you were doing.<br /> <br /> Boons are also only needed when you want to be able to always* do something, and not have it be an every once in a while kind of thing for your character.<br /> <br /> *For varying degrees of always, some boons still require legend to be spent.<br /> <br /> You seem to want to play in a super heroes game, which is fine, but Scion is not a super hero game. Legendary Items, Followers, Guides, Creatures, and their relationship with you character speak to the Mythic origins of the Scions, and having a lightning bolt that allows you to control the weather and fly is perfectly in line with the type of game that Scion is going for.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry that this game isn't for you, but no game is for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 03-19-2018, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T17:21:54-07:00","id":1197396,"title":"","content":"If we assume rough parallelism between the tiers of play in Trinity and Scion (at least in terms relative scale), \u201cAberrant\u201d Era Novas are the character type in Trinity that go for the type of supers play Irioth is describing, and they\u2019re Tier 3 - which would correspond to Demigod for Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T17:55:49-07:00","id":1197410,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with Irioth that it feels a lot smaller than I was hoping, and I was just hoping it would match the scope of 1E Scion at the Hero level. Unfortunately the characters I've been able to come up with so far feel a lot more limited than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T17:57:51-07:00","id":1197413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197396#post1197396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we assume rough parallelism between the tiers of play in Trinity and Scion (at least in terms relative scale), \u201cAberrant\u201d Era Novas are the character type in Trinity that go for the type of supers play Irioth is describing, and they\u2019re Tier 3 - which would correspond to Demigod for Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is the source of my frustration. I pledged to the KS in the expectation that street-level action-adventure Origin type of play would be useless and distasteful to my tastes, but I could skip it entirely except as it concerns using the book for the basic ruleset (kinda like the CoD corebook is a prop for the Mage or Beast games I fancy), and jump directly into Hero, where I'd be able to play properly superhuman, divinely-empowered characters, recognizable equivalents of Heracles or Sun Wukong, or if you wish the Avatar, not glorified Bronze Age elites that may use a supernatural trick or two once in a great while, in the modern age. At the beginning of their careers and with several rough edges no doubt, but with a recognizable superhuman stature and set of abilities nonetheless. Then Demigod and God would allow me to play the same concepts hovering at the verge of, and fully plunging into, world-shaking transcendence, if you wish the rough equivalent of Marvel's Thor becoming king of Asgard and inheriting the Odinpower (only w/o Odin necessarily dying, or maybe so depending on how the Titanomachy turned out). Now I discover I was misled by the expectations an optimistic notion of &quot;awesome children of the gods on a journey to join their ranks&quot; created, I absolutely need at least Demigod (maybe) to play the kind of game I like, the money I invested in the Hero KS is entirely wasted, short of waiting for a second KS and pair of books that are not even on the horizon. That Origin and Hero may have been a necessary stepping stone for Demigod and God to be created is very cold comfort when the latter two are not even in the first draft stage (and development of the first two books took considerably longer than expected).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-19-2018, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T18:20:27-07:00","id":1197417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197410#post1197410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree with Irioth that it feels a lot smaller than I was hoping, and I was just hoping it would match the scope of 1E Scion at the Hero level. Unfortunately the characters I've been able to come up with so far feel a lot more limited than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. If you ask my opnion, there is something seriously wrong if these supposed 'children of the gods' can reliably do but a tiny fraction of what mages, beasts, vampires, etc. do all the time without even trying hard. The game concept creates expectations, and its realization in hard rules terms feels so limited and cognitively dissonant as to make the game unplayable, at least for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-19-2018, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T18:28:45-07:00","id":1197420,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking so far everything is still kept more or less on a grounded level. Isn't that where we'd expect Origins/Hero to be? I mean the character/s are still figuring things out. They should feel limited because they aren't gods, or even demigods yet. Their still making their own legends, building their own stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T18:37:22-07:00","id":1197426,"title":"","content":"I get it\u2019s not what you wanted and I completely respect that. I\u2019m just unclear on what you thought the Hero/Demigod tier distinction were going to be, since obviously the fact that said tiers existed were advertised. For a tiered game like this to work off of myth, there needs to be a tier where Achilles, Odysseus, Beowulf, and the Fianna hang out - or where Heracles starts when he\u2019s just strangling monsters and not holding up the sky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T18:57:38-07:00","id":1197437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197426#post1197426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get it\u2019s not what you wanted and I completely respect that. I\u2019m just unclear on what you thought the Hero/Demigod tier distinction were going to be, since obviously the fact that said tiers existed were advertised. For a tiered game like this to work off of myth, there needs to be a tier where Achilles, Odysseus, Beowulf, and the Fianna hang out - or where Heracles starts when he\u2019s just strangling monsters and not holding up the sky.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expected the 'top human potential' action-adventure Achilles/Beowulf type of play would be strictly Origins, and by Hero we would clearly progress in the Hercules/Sun Wukong stage when the average character is recognizably all-around superhuman and reliably punches out or blasts true monsters mortals are powerless against, and by Demigod we'd be in the &quot;hero changes the world as routine quest&quot; holding up the sky type of play. As I see it, Hero is just like Origins, except for the frustrating window dressing of a few (an handful at most if you optimize within an inch of your life) D&amp;D magic and Hollywood blockbuster tricks you may use once in a great while without crippling the character for the rest of the session. Stuff your average CoD supernatural can do without breaking a sweat.<br /> <br /> So I'd expect I'd get Origins to work like the CoD rulebook, and Hero to work like VtR, WtF, MtAw, or BtP, only more awesome. Instead I got the Special Forces game, and the Ghouls game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-19-2018, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T19:12:11-07:00","id":1197444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197410#post1197410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree with Irioth that it feels a lot smaller than I was hoping, and I was just hoping it would match the scope of 1E Scion at the Hero level. Unfortunately the characters I've been able to come up with so far feel a lot more limited than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That because in 1e it was practically mandatory to start at Legend 4, and this game doesn't allow for that as a default option. Starting at Hero in Scion 2e players are still quite powerful. Far more so then characters starting at Legend 2 back in 1e, and once they get some xp under their belt, they are actually more powerful then 1e. (Not factoring in the BS that was Epic Attributes)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197413#post1197413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whiny stuff about how &quot;Bronze Age&quot; Heroes are exactly what the Scion: Hero game allows, and not Demigods or Gods</div> </div> </div> </div>At Character Creation a Hero has: 5-7 Knacks (No Mortal Knacks require Legend Expenditure, and very few require Momentum, most are therefore always on or available), 2 Purviews (Minimum) with the associated Innate Powers, 2 Boons, and 7-11 points of Birthrights (Which may give you access to their own Knacks, or Purviews even, and therefore grant additional Innate Powers). That's not even taking into account what Miracles actually allow you to achieve, and how easy it is to get back Spent Legend in 2e. All in all, Heroic characters are actually quite a bit beyond Mortal, and in a good place for them to start building their Legends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197417#post1197417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More whining about what the &quot;children of the gods&quot; can do vs &quot;mages, beasts, vampires, etc&quot; without really understanding just how little 3 discipline dots, or gift will get you vs everything that a starting Scion is capable of, because instead of trying to see what they can actually do, he has focused on what they can't do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could try and reason with you. I could try and &quot;prove&quot; to you how much power Hero's have available to them, but I don't think I'm going to waste my time beating my head against that particular wall. It's obvious that you've made up your mind, and while I can lead a man to knowledge, I can not make him think. So all I will say is &quot;So long.&quot; and &quot;I hope you find a game out there that is more to your tastes.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T19:30:09-07:00","id":1197453,"title":"","content":"A Scion with one Fire Boon can gain the ability to hurl limitless fireballs at his/her enemies for an entire scene. He/she loses nothing from doing this. <br /> <br /> A Scion with Fertility can curse or bless an entire genetic lineage with a simple action or cause an entire region to have an insane bumper crop.<br /> <br /> A Scion with Frost can freeze multiple enemies solid with a simple gesture. <br /> <br /> HOW exactly are Heroes weak again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T20:12:56-07:00","id":1197460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197453#post1197453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Scion with one Fire Boon can gain the ability to hurl limitless fireballs at his/her enemies for an entire scene. He/she loses nothing from doing this.</div> </div> </div> </div>To my frustrated checking, this is pretty much the only ranged-attack kind of Boon that does not require Legend expenditure. One exception does not make the rule. As much as Fire is one of my preferred elemental powers ever, I'd rather prefer not be forced to include the Fire Purview in the powerset of each and every combat-worthy Scion to have one reliable, reusable supernatural ranged attack option. If the other elemental combat-worthy Boons, or the ones representing other vanilla magical feats such as healing or shapeshifting, did not require to spend Legend too, you'd hear me complain a lot less about the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Scion with Fertility can curse or bless an entire genetic lineage with a simple action or cause an entire region to have an insane bumper crop. </div> </div> </div>[sarcasm]Oh yeah, I'm sure this is going to be super useful in average play. [/sarcasm]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Scion with Frost can freeze multiple enemies solid with a simple gesture. </div> </div> </div>And get their ability to use any other noteworthy supernatural power crippled for the rest of the session, like a low-level Vancian magic user. Pass.<br /> <br /> You know what really feels impressive, in the &quot;badass supernatural being&quot; sense? A Begotten being able to do this kind of stuff all day long, without making a dent in their mystical juice reserves, and much, much more with a few dozen Xp invested in Atavisms, Merits, and Nightmares from the corebook alone, while Scions are doomed to stay nailed in the same exact place, give or take an handful extra tricks, no matter how long you play the character till Demigod gets written. Let's not even get started about what the Awakened can do with a few moderately developed Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-19-2018, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T21:14:09-07:00","id":1197478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197368#post1197368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I came to this game expecting I would be able to play a divinely empowered if still somewhat inexperienced high-tier comic-book or anime superhero, say Avatar Korra at the beginning of her series,</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to sound rude or anything, but why? What part of hero's advertising made you think that? To my knowledge hero has always been 'normal mortal with a bit of divine oomph behind them' and things only started getting crazier at upper legends. Hell as far back as the sardonyx teasers when scale was first introduced, hero is put at around psion level and the actual super heros are said to be at god tier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T21:43:55-07:00","id":1197482,"title":"","content":"I have some of the same issues, and said months ago that I was worried about too much emphasis being on mortals and low-level stuff in a game that is supposed to be about playing much, much larger-than-life characters. Yes, you have to start somewhere - but this is a game designed, promoted, and anticipated to be about GODS. It should feel &quot;wow, I can do that?&quot;, not &quot;seriously, that's all I can do?&quot; And so far, it's underwhelming for what it was designed to be. Yes, this is Scion, a game about playing the heroes and Gods of the great legends. We should expect to be able to do big, cool stuff, because that's what the myths are about. &quot;Don't reveal yourself, you might get fatebound&quot;, &quot;don't lose your birthright macguffin or you lose power and daddy gets mad&quot;, don't use your cool power now, because you won't get to use it later&quot; is the opposite of legendary. The source material about the Gods is cool and well-done. The system is underwhelming. And as has been pointed out, we have no release schedule at all for Demigod and God. So far, I'm just not blown away with what I see. It isn't bad. It's just...too small for the source material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T21:47:15-07:00","id":1197484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197460#post1197460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To my frustrated checking, this is pretty much the only ranged-attack kind of Boon that does not require Legend expenditure. One exception does not make the rule. As much as Fire is one of my preferred elemental powers ever, I'd rather prefer not be forced to include the Fire Purview in the powerset of each and every combat-worthy Scion to have one reliable, reusable supernatural ranged attack option. If the other elemental combat-worthy Boons, or the ones representing other vanilla magical feats such as healing or shapeshifting, did not require to spend Legend too, you'd hear me complain a lot less about the system.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Fire Boon is essentially just giving you a fancy weapon. The others are full-fledged area of effect attacks that hit everything in Range at once. They are definitely powerful enough to cost Legend, and are not powers you should be throwing around willy-nilly at Hero level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197460#post1197460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [sarcasm]Oh yeah, I'm sure this is going to be super useful in average play. [/sarcasm]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you can't see the blackmail potential in a power that lets you essentially wipe out a target's bloodline my making all conceptions and pregnancies fail, and that slowly kills off all their child and elderly relatives, then I can't help you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197460#post1197460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And get their ability to use any other noteworthy supernatural power crippled for the rest of the session, like a low-level Vancian magic user. Pass.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Fatebonds are for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197460#post1197460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know what really feels impressive, in the &quot;badass supernatural being&quot; sense? A Begotten being able to do this kind of stuff all day long, without making a dent in their mystical juice reserves, and much, much more with a few dozen Xp invested in Atavisms, Merits, and Nightmares from the corebook alone, while Scions are doomed to stay nailed in the same exact place, give or take an handful extra tricks, no matter how long you play the character till Demigod gets written. Let's not even get started about what the Awakened can do with a few moderately developed Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Beasts and Mages are pitifully weak compared to starting Nobles from Nobilis. What's your point? That the characters from two different gamelines that have no actual connection to each other have different power sets? Gasp!<br /> <br /> To comment on just one point you made though, Scion is a game about mythology... mythology is replete with Heroes that gain power from items familiars mentors and followers... having a lot of your power come from them is not a bug, it's a feature. And please don't forget that Korra is literally unique... there is only one Avatar, all the other Benders are single element. She's the exception, not the rule, of what Heroes. As for Hercules, most of what he did is completely possible with Hunter Warrior and investment in the Epic Physicals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T21:54:28-07:00","id":1197485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197478#post1197478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to sound rude or anything, but why? What part of hero's advertising made you think that? To my knowledge hero has always been 'normal mortal with a bit of divine oomph behind them' and things only started getting crazier at upper legends. Hell as far back as the sardonyx teasers when scale was first introduced, hero is put at around psion level and the actual super heros are said to be at god tier.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said above, I suppose the splitting of Origin and Hero gave me an exaggerated impression of the latter's power level, Besides, I did not really pay any attention to the sardonyx teasers, I only came around for the KS itself, and to my memory this element was not really stressed enough during the KS process for me to notice (otherwise I'd have been a much more reluctant patron, or none at all). Anyway, I'm certainly annoying to have wasted $105, but only that much. This is not the first nor I suspect the last KS project that failed to deliver for me, one way or another, What really leaves me frustrated is there is a lot of ideas I love in this game, but the insufficient power level is far too much of an impssable annoyance to me. What might well be the remedy, Demigod and God, is stll years in the making, and I'm an impatient guy. And there is a fair dearth of options in the RPG genre to suit my tastes for playing this concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T21:55:23-07:00","id":1197486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197482#post1197482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some of the same issues, and said months ago that I was worried about too much emphasis being on mortals and low-level stuff in a game that is supposed to be about playing much, much larger-than-life characters. Yes, you have to start somewhere - but this is a game designed, promoted, and anticipated to be about GODS.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it was designed, promoted and anticipated to be about the mortal children and chosen of Gods. Scion : God is the book for playing Gods. That's not even me trying to be impertinent, I'm honestly trying to point out that Hero was always meant to be the lowest tier of Godly power, and even that is pretty impressive in ability.. Heroes are more limited in the narrowness of their areas of specialization, but they can be absolutely devastating there. You need to have somewhere to go up to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T22:09:28-07:00","id":1197487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197482#post1197482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some of the same issues, and said months ago that I was worried about too much emphasis being on mortals and low-level stuff in a game that is supposed to be about playing much, much larger-than-life characters. Yes, you have to start somewhere - but this is a game designed, promoted, and anticipated to be about GODS. It should feel &quot;wow, I can do that?&quot;, not &quot;seriously, that's all I can do?&quot; And so far, it's underwhelming for what it was designed to be. Yes, this is Scion, a game about playing the heroes and Gods of the great legends. We should expect to be able to do big, cool stuff, because that's what the myths are about. &quot;Don't reveal yourself, you might get fatebound&quot;, &quot;don't lose your birthright macguffin or you lose power and daddy gets mad&quot;, don't use your cool power now, because you won't get to use it later&quot; is the opposite of legendary. The source material about the Gods is cool and well-done. The system is underwhelming. And as has been pointed out, we have no release schedule at all for Demigod and God. So far, I'm just not blown away with what I see. It isn't bad. It's just...too small for the source material.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you think the Fianna, Perseus, etc etc aren't examples of a vast genre of myths that Hero was advertised around emulating, I really don't know what to tell you.<br /> <br /> If anything Hero level Scions have vastly more power than is mythically accurate to their source material in order to make it more fun to play and in response to superhero-inflated audience expectations. The mortal offspring of Zeus do not typically have the option to control the weather or fly, for example. Magic artifacts are generally how divine-blooded heroes got to do overtly magical things. Innate Purviews is an expansion beyond that (though also necessary because 2E treats Epic Attributes as Purviews)<br /> <br /> <br /> Can you give me an example of a divine-blooded mortal Hero that you feel the rules for &quot;Hero&quot; do not allow you to capture?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T22:42:15-07:00","id":1197490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197484#post1197484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fire Boon is essentially just giving you a fancy weapon. The others are full-fledged area of effect attacks that hit everything in Range at once. They are definitely powerful enough to cost Legend, and are not powers you should be throwing around willy-nilly at Hero level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't the other kinds of elemental scions have their own fancy weapons? Why not have a general standard that all damaging Boons only cost Legend if they are area of effect, or are &quot;I win&quot; instantly incapacitating buttons? Would have been too difficult to add a rule option that such Boons imbue Legend if they are single-target, and cost Legend if they upgrade to area of effect?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you can't see the blackmail potential in a power that lets you essentially wipe out a target's bloodline my making all conceptions and pregnancies fail, and that slowly kills off all their child and elderly relatives, then I can't help you. </div> </div> </div>Given what is expected to be the usual kind of play in this game, I'd chalk this as hardcore niche use. Really, how often should one expect to see &quot;do as I say or I'll make your bloodline sterile&quot; blackmail in mythos, ancient or modern?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's what Fatebonds are for. </div> </div> </div>How often can one expect to rack Fatebonds, before they become disruptive to story flaw, and the character unmanageable. I was under the impression the threshold was once every few sesssions at most.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To comment on just one point you made though, Scion is a game about mythology... mythology is replete with Heroes that gain power from items familiars mentors and followers... having a lot of your power come from them is not a bug, it's a feature. And please don't forget that Korra is literally unique... there is only one Avatar, all the other Benders are single element. She's the exception, not the rule, of what Heroes. As for Hercules, most of what he did is completely possible with Hunter Warrior and investment in the Epic Physicals. </div> </div> </div>My main issue with this is the inherent nature of my character's powers to be safely contained in their very bodies or minds is an essential feature of my gaming fun. I cannot stand the idea of abilities being dependent on items that can be lost, destroyed, or stolen. My default solution for this in Hero terms would be to strictly define all Purview-bestowing Relics of my characters as stuff that cannot be really be lost or stolen in normal circumstances, Pantheon cultural flavor be thrice damned, such as tattooes, techno-magic cybernetics, scarifications, or jewels embedded in the character's body, or at the very least stuff that is worn such as rings, necklaces, bracers, belts, earrings, and the like, rather than stuff that is carried or yielded. &quot;I lost the item that channels my powers&quot; is simply not a subplot I'm willing to play in any game. And I'be very, very careful to stay in my Guide's good graces. My character need to be thrown naked in a cell, or travel with their clothes alone, and retain 90% of their abilities, and have to be unable to think, or at least speak or gesture, effectively to lose access to their powers. Rest assured that once I got Hero I checked the Relic (and Guide) rules, to be sure I'd be able to define my own access to Purviews this way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T22:44:53-07:00","id":1197491,"title":"","content":"Well...again not to sound rude, but it sounds to me like you really just have yourself to blame for your disappointment. Not really sure what the point of posting about it here is honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T22:51:27-07:00","id":1197493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197487#post1197487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you think the Fianna, Perseus, etc etc aren't examples of a vast genre of myths that Hero was advertised around emulating, I really don't know what to tell you.<br /> <br /> If anything Hero level Scions have vastly more power than is mythically accurate to their source material in order to make it more fun to play and in response to superhero-inflated audience expectations. The mortal offspring of Zeus do not typically have the option to control the weather or fly, for example. Magic artifacts are generally how divine-blooded heroes got to do overtly magical things. Innate Purviews is an expansion beyond that (though also necessary because 2E treats Epic Attributes as Purviews)<br /> <br /> <br /> Can you give me an example of a divine-blooded mortal Hero that you feel the rules for &quot;Hero&quot; do not allow you to capture?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the modern age. In the face of modern technology, an helluva lot of what might look sufficiently impressive to qualify for Bronze Age mythology feels entirely boring and mundane now, and modern legends need to adapt to stay relevant. In so many ways, superheroics are modern mythology, and the stories of gods and their offspring in the modern age need be channled through their lens to fit. The original feats of the Fianna and Perseus? Nothing a grunt with a M-16 cannot easily dispose of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-20-2018, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T23:02:24-07:00","id":1197497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197490#post1197490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often can one expect to rack Fatebonds, before they become disruptive to story flaw, and the character unmanageable. I was under the impression the threshold was once every few sesssions at most.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to ignore the rest of what you said and focus on this misconception right here. You can gain a fatebinding if you so choose once per session. You can also compel it for another fate point, once per session. This binding will be Strength 1, and will therefore go away at the end of the game session unless you do something to lengthen its duration. So, right there, 2 Legend points per session. So, at Legend 1, adding in the 2 &quot;free&quot; Legend points per game session, without going into anything complicated, drastic, or long lasting, that gives you up to 3 Spent, let alone imbued, Legend per session. How many scenes of &quot;Whatever the hell I need it to be, that loosely falls under one of my Purviews, that is not already covered my one of my Knacks, Innate Powers, or Boons&quot; do you feel that you need in any given game session?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":".  Minor Sacrifices are once per arc, not per session. Though they are available every few sessions if you really need the juice to burn. 03-20-2018, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T23:38:51-07:00","id":1197501,"title":"","content":"I'll just gently step in and mention that the Boon List in Hero is not meant to be an ironclad list. Like... You can <i>make</i> more Boons.<br /> <br /> There's literally nothing stopping you from taking the Throwing Fire Boon and filing the serial numbers off to make it throwing weaker lightning bolts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 03-20-2018, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T00:14:02-07:00","id":1197505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197493#post1197493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the modern age. In the face of modern technology, an helluva lot of what might look sufficiently impressive to qualify for Bronze Age mythology feels entirely boring and mundane now, and modern legends need to adapt to stay relevant. In so many ways, superheroics are modern mythology, and the stories of gods and their offspring in the modern age need be channled through their lens to fit. The original feats of the Fianna and Perseus? Nothing a grunt with a M-16 cannot easily dispose of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well then yeah, it was pretty ridiculous for you to have spent money on a game to play a character concept that you don't like the core premise of - that's 100% on you though, not a failure on the game's part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T05:28:37-07:00","id":1197567,"title":"","content":"A grunt with an M16 would be turned to stone within secondsof setting foot in Medusa's lair. He DEFINITELY would be useless against the sea monster. <br /> <br /> The ability to throw fireballs, call down lightning, drain people's life force, and wither an entire genetic lineage are still more than impressive enough in modern times. Heck except for the fireballs, modern technology STILL can't match those feats. Oh! And then there's the Chaos Purview, which can render most technology (and the people who use it) non-functional. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197501#post1197501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll just gently step in and mention that the Boon List in Hero is not meant to be an ironclad list. Like... You can <i>make</i> more Boons.<br /> <br /> There's literally nothing stopping you from taking the Throwing Fire Boon and filing the serial numbers off to make it throwing weaker lightning bolts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, this. Feel free to make up your own Boons that fit with your very narrow &quot;Must be able to crush entire modern armies between bites of my morning cronut&quot; motif.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T07:05:44-07:00","id":1197585,"title":"","content":"I don't have a specific legendary hero in mind as an example, because I wouldn't run a game with the intent of playing Antiope or Cu Cullainne. It's about creating and playing your own myths and legends. In essence, this feels to me like, &quot;here's a game about super-heroes. But the first book is just about playing your mortal secret identity. The second book, that's for when you first learn that you have powers, but can't really do super stuff. (and sorry, &quot;I doom your future generations&quot; is legitimate, but not something that would fit into an action-and-adventure tale very well) The third and fourth books, the ones that actually let you be superheroes, they won't be out for a year or two.&quot; It fixed broken stuff from 1st edition, but really seems to have nerfed powers a bit too much. And if you have limited uses, that leads to, &quot;well, I won't use my power now, I might need it later. Or now, because I might need it in the next encounter. Oh, shit, the mission's over and I never used my cool power.&quot; It's not just about simulating myths, it's about <i>feeling </i>like you're part of a bigger adventure. So far, despite cool ideas and good mythological information, I'm still disappointed that it' starting off too slowly. Maybe in 2021, when I have all the books, I'll see it differently. But right now, I'm sadly underwhelmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T07:20:05-07:00","id":1197593,"title":"","content":"<i>Trinity</i> is the game about playing modern superheroes. <br /> <br /> <i>Scion</i> is about playing thousand year old stories in modern times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T07:25:36-07:00","id":1197595,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that random human mooks are almost certainly trivial targets, and therefore you can do whatever you goddamn want to them basically free with Purviews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T07:26:36-07:00","id":1197597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197585#post1197585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... In essence, this feels to me like, &quot;here's a game about super-heroes....</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is where we're having our fundamental difference of opinion... I didn't go into Scion expecting a game about superheroes... And neither did it ever advertise itself as one. It's a game about playing the heroes of myth, in the modern day... And it simulates that quite well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I do love superheroes too though, which is why I also backed Trinity... I would suggest you check it out, it might give you what you're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 03-20-2018, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T07:36:27-07:00","id":1197600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197505#post1197505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well then yeah, it was pretty ridiculous for you to have spent money on a game to play a character concept that you don't like the core premise of - that's 100% on you though, not a failure on the game's part.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, I've reached the conclusion Origin and Hero can only be relevant, interesting, and useful to me the same way the TC rulebook, the psion book, and the CotD rulebook are for Aberrant and Mage/Beast/Vampire respectively: generic rules source and completist setting detail for the other games I fancy, not something I'd ever want to play on its own. A bit overpriced for me to get them this way instead of say grabbing them when a discount is available on Drivethrough and/or I feel like a wealthy collectionist (not to mention more... unorthodox sources), but alas wrong purchases are a fact of life. What is left to me about Scion is to gaze in the future, collect clues about Demigod and God, and try to puzzle out if those projects at least can truly fulfill my tastes or there is something in the makeup of the gameline that would taint the entire project to me. Not a near future concern, since they are neither in the release schedule nor their KS is on the horizon.<br /> <br /> At least with the TC project I was entirely aware of where I stood with the gameline since the old edition: I was in it 100% for Aberrant (and I loved it despite its serious flaws), I couldn't care less about Trinity (actually, being a transhumanist Teragen fanboy, I actively hated what the psion game stood for and cheerleaded for alternate versions of the timeline where Divis Mal's army smashes the bloody Muggle conspiracies to bits and seizes the destiny of mankind) and Adventure except as a minor source of setting info. So I was in the whole TC project only as it concerns indirectly helping get the new Aberrant book eventually written. I suppose I should have picked the same exact attitude about Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-20-2018, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T07:42:51-07:00","id":1197602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197593#post1197593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Trinity</i> is the game about playing modern superheroes.<br /> <br /> <i>Scion</i> is about playing thousand year old stories in modern times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, no. If the old edition is anything to go by, Aberrant is about playing modern superheroes. Trinity is about playing low-powered psionic versions of the Sentinels in the far future. If one cares about playing superheroes, they should be aware of how the various games of the TC line radically diverge in their intended power level and approach to superheroics, in order to avoid a(nother) disillusionement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-20-2018, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T08:27:42-07:00","id":1197613,"title":"","content":"Trinity is being used here as shorthand for \u201cTrinity Continuum\u201d, as opposed to \u201cthe Trinity RPG\u201d. As such, it's inclusive of the TC core, TC: \u00c6on, TC: Aberrant, TC: Adventure, and any other books set in the Trinity Continuum (e.g., TC: \u00c6gis and TC: Anima). The point being made was that the Trinity Continuum is the shared reality designed to handle superheroes, not the Scion gamelines. It's literally true, though in a larger sense it isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T08:44:31-07:00","id":1197621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197613#post1197613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trinity is being used here as shorthand for \u201cTrinity Continuum\u201d, as opposed to \u201cthe Trinity RPG\u201d. As such, it's inclusive of the TC core, TC: \u00c6on, TC: Aberrant, TC: Adventure, and any other books set in the Trinity Continuum (e.g., TC: \u00c6gis and TC: Anima). The point being made was that the Trinity Continuum is the shared reality designed to handle superheroes, not the Scion gamelines. It's literally true, though in a larger sense it isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>True in a sense, although within that shared reality one still needs be aware of the radical design differences between the various games. If one wants to play recognizable superheroics (mixed with the effects of celebrity culture and warring conspiracies) they need to be careful picking the game that actually is about modern superhumans, as opposed to the one about their far future alien-empowered psion hunters (or other parts of the franchise I'm less aware of). The point is relevant since a big part of this discussion has been about how the different design philosophies of various parts of the Scion gameline impact play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-20-2018, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T09:25:38-07:00","id":1197644,"title":"","content":"Adventure! deals with pulp fiction; \u00c6gis deals with the heroes, sorcerers and (demi?)gods of ancient Greece; and Anima deals with a time shortly after the Aberrant War and before the rise of the psions when mentally intrusive hardtech ran rampant. But your point is taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T11:19:56-07:00","id":1197687,"title":"","content":"Between boons (and innate powers), knacks (mortal and immortal), birthrights, there's plenty of power for a hero to craft his/her legend to me. (And the gods help any vampire, werewolf, or mage that gets in the way) And lets not forget ...the hero still has a connection to his/her godly parent)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T12:21:28-07:00","id":1197703,"title":"","content":"I would argue that there is very little difference between legendary heroes and super-heroes. They are empowered beings who do grand deeds, battle powerful foes, and change the course of history. The difference is in the setting and narrative, not the underlying concept. But that's really a topic for another thread. The issue here is that, in my opinion, this game so far has not made me feel the grand scope that I think it should. It may do so for you, and that's great, but it hasn't done it for me. One person's opinion, subject to possible revision at a later date, when more material is available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T14:24:58-07:00","id":1197740,"title":"","content":"gee, and I thought it was a Role Playing Game, as in a game were you play a ROLE based on the setting the GM (or DM, or Marshal, or ST, or whatever you want to call them) created. the power level of any game, regardless of anything else, is up to the person behind the screen. yes both sides have valid points, but the point should never be, it's not powerful enough for me, instead it should be, &quot;Is this interesting to my players&quot;. Irioth you said one of the most important thing in this discussion, and no one noticed. &quot;<b>there is a lot of ideas I love in this game</b>&quot;. and that is what any game is, ideas. use the ideas, forget about the &quot;rules&quot; and let what you read spark your imagination and use that!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12529-nico-diangelo","name":"Nico diAngelo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12529_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T14:40:58-07:00","id":1197749,"title":"","content":"It's a small thing but I have to note that thinking &quot;Oh snap i'm gonna play Sun Wukong&quot; at Hero tier is a bit of a mistake, as Sun Wukong came out of his egg with laser eyes and with minimal training was strong enough to lift the 17,550 pound size-changing pillar that he went on to use as a staff. IIRC, 90% of the problems in Journey to the West were solved with &quot;Throw Monkey at it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sun Wukong shouldn't be anybody's idea of what constitutes Hero Tier. Dude was smashing through Heaven and beating down the strongest immortals the Kingdom of Heaven could field before he was conscripted to take the titular Journey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T15:24:59-07:00","id":1197760,"title":"","content":"I just re-read the Bolt from the Blue writeup. That Boon deals Aggravated damage to all targets within a certain range band and you can buy it at freaking Character Creation! <br /> <br /> Name another game in which you can gain the power to do Area of Effect Aggravated damage right from the jump?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T16:02:05-07:00","id":1197770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197760#post1197760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just re-read the Bolt from the Blue writeup. That Boon deals Aggravated damage to all targets within a certain range band and you can buy it at freaking Character Creation! <br /> <br /> Name another game in which you can gain the power to do Area of Effect Aggravated damage right from the jump?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavenly Fire does Aggravated as well, with the limitation of you can only hit one target at once with it.<br /> <br /> There's also the Tsunami Water Boon that hits with what, Highest Force + Athletics + 4e? All in a range, with Shockwave.<br /> <br /> Spending Legend will wipe the map.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T20:58:46-07:00","id":1197874,"title":"","content":"One of my issues is the Orisha's Flaw. It doesn't feel like a flaw, not like the other Pantheon's flaws. Where the others feel like a flaw from within, theirs feels like a hurdle from without. (I hope that makes sense)<br /> <br /> In example. The Shen, their flaw is the fact there are so many they are overwhelming their own Celestial Bureaucracy.<br /> The Theoi, they are more often stepping on each other's toes, distracting them from their battle in the Titanomachy.<br /> The Tuatha are bound by Geas, their greatest strength is their greatest weakness.<br /> The Manitou have incredible (almost ungodly) amount of pride.<br /> The Deva are arrogant and large, using their numbers and power to rest on.<br /> The Aseir have their apples (drugs), their all too human fears of dying and getting old.<br /> The Kami are also proud and arrogant.<br /> The Netjer have infighting, everyone has the same tasks as about four others, there's confusion and arguments about who does what and when.<br /> The Teotl, their crutch of faith and sacrifice of their followers is their biggest flaw.<br /> <br /> All are Flaws from within, the only one that is close to being a flaw from without is the Teotl. As they are relying on the acts of their worshipers for energy and power, yet they need it to simply be, much like the Aseir and their Golden Apples.<br /> <br /> I feel the Orisha were building to a different flaw. One of distrust of other Gods, keeping them at arm\u2019s length, and only trusting them AFTER they have done something to prove they are not going to harm them in the ways they have been before. After all, given what they have done to survive, even changing some of their own identities and grow into the Loa I feel they would be much, much more like the Wakanada people in the Black Panther movie. Or even their ideal of NOT FIGHTING the Titans, as they simply have not dealt with one, maybe more of a minor flaw than anything. A level of naive understanding of Titans perhaps, or simply being on the outside looking in?<br /> <br /> Then, you have the later chapter that talks about approaching rough and visceral themes like racism and sexism with respect and understanding that some people wouldn\u2019t want to talk about that in detail. It\u2019s odd to see a weakness being something so in your face, then being told to step back from it. It limits the Role Play potential, where a Distrust Flaw would be much easier to RP and have more often around. That is what my Orisha will have as their main character flaw, I disagree with the presented Flaw as is. Beyond that, I do enjoy the character of each, it's well done and impressive. With that one blemish, that is my only real issue. It feels......backwards from the other set of flaws presented.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24011-ivoryknight22","name":"Ivoryknight22","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T17:32:02-07:00","id":1198907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1197600#post1197600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...(not to mention more... unorthodox sources)...</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bLet's not be making veiled references to piracy, please and thank you.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T20:55:34-07:00","id":1198954,"title":"","content":"I do admit I also feel a tad underpowered but I can see that we're not supposed to reach the top tier yet. Though is there any way to advance boon or Knack count without gaining legend?<br /> I do wish I could multitask a bit more with the boons but I guess that's something for higher legend play.<br /> <br /> Do we have an ETA on the companion book? After reading the relics section it has made want more info on creating one with my character and it says that such info will be in companion.<br /> <br /> I also agree that the weakness of the Orisha honestly feels pretty terrible compared to the weakness of the other pantheons. I get racism pretty bad but they seem almost pathetic in the fact that their fall was due to just mortals alone completely without a titan or something sabotaging them. It mentions that other faiths went through similar hardships and yet they are the ones that have that as their weakness/flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T06:52:20-07:00","id":1199027,"title":"","content":"You can have more Knacks than you us and just swap them around between sessions, and to get the Boon fix, I imagine you could get a lot of mileage out of Marvels.<br /> <br /> As for the \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0, I think part of it is the sheer magnitude of the atrocities committed to their people, and the fact that even gods themselves were not immune to the actions of the slave trade and exploitation (also, I find it interesting that the \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0 don't really believe in &quot;Titans&quot;, so instead they get hammered by the most powerful force in The World: Fate). Considering the influence Fatebinding had in reshaping their pantheon, I could see an argument that one of the reasons their weakness is massive systemic racism and religious intolerance is that they are *still* being hammered by the Fate hammer, treating them as being lesser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T09:30:12-07:00","id":1199088,"title":"","content":"Hmf...I can't imagine feeling underpowered when the comparisons are typically against human mortals.<br /> You begin with a concept that tells you what skills you already have.<br /> Then get that &quot;visit&quot; which wakes up your abilities, and sometimes get a gift or two. <br /> Then there's the three paths; Origin, Role, and Pantheon, where three skills per path kick in.<br /> And you start off with one dot in each attribute. And begin with three knacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T12:56:40-07:00","id":1199455,"title":"","content":"After reading back on Origins it does alleviate some of my worries with regards to underpoweredness, I missed a few things that actually gave more perspective on the gap between Hero and Origins tier. <br /> <br /> Though I am curious as to how other cultures split souls up after seeing the Orisha and Netjer describe the various parts of the soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T16:03:25-07:00","id":1199519,"title":"","content":"Is there an example Boon I missed for shifting ones sexual morphology? If not, what Purview would you put it under? I\u2019m thinking Moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T16:10:28-07:00","id":1199521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1199519#post1199519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an example Boon I missed for shifting ones sexual morphology? If not, what Purview would you put it under? I\u2019m thinking Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitively metamorphisis. Aside from that, i'd like to say ... fertility maybe??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T16:34:43-07:00","id":1199526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1199521#post1199521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitively metamorphisis. Aside from that, i'd like to say ... fertility maybe??</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly Metamorphosis, but I meant for everyone who isn\u2019t Theoi.<br /> <br /> Fertility makes sense as it\u2019s by that power that Scions of Inari would do so.<br /> <br /> I was thinking Moon because of its age changing magic, so it would fit the shifting phases theme.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m left wondering what the mechanics basis for Loki\u2019s shapeshifting is, since obviously it\u2019s far greater than any other Aesir, and it\u2019s not like they have Metamorphosis or even have the Beast purview for potentially calling on animal forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T17:00:18-07:00","id":1199537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1199526#post1199526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m left wondering what the mechanics basis for Loki\u2019s shapeshifting is, since obviously it\u2019s far greater than any other Aesir, and it\u2019s not like they have Metamorphosis or even have the Beast purview for potentially calling on animal forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>My best guess would be through an unusual application of either the Deception purview or the Trickster calling. Basically &quot;pretending to be an animal&quot; elevated to godly proportions. Also, it may occasionally be just for color - for instance, becoming a walrus for a wrestling dispute might just be a visual representation of applying his Epic Strength (particularly if he is using a Boon or Marvel to allow a Feat of Scale on said wrestling).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T17:01:13-07:00","id":1199538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1199526#post1199526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Certainly Metamorphosis, but I meant for everyone who isn\u2019t Theoi.<br /> <br /> Fertility makes sense as it\u2019s by that power that Scions of Inari would do so.<br /> <br /> I was thinking Moon because of its age changing magic, so it would fit the shifting phases theme.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m left wondering what the mechanics basis for Loki\u2019s shapeshifting is, since obviously it\u2019s far greater than any other Aesir, and it\u2019s not like they have Metamorphosis or even have the Beast purview for potentially calling on animal forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>One can figure out a way to do it via some justification. <br /> <br /> Loki I figure could get away with his shapeshifting via the Chaos purview or the Deception Purview. <br /> Something about Chaos applying to his very form and not be restrained to the order of having a singular appearance. <br /> Deception could have it so that all his shapeshifting was him altering the perception and memory of those around him. That or possibly him lying to reality/fate so hard his lies became true, not capable of warping the rest of the world but only that which he has total control of, himself. <br /> Or due to the fact that apparently every myth is true and one can ignore the rules if you see a cool enough justification just state that he's an exception among the Aesir and capable of actually attaining the Metamorphosis purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T20:11:00-07:00","id":1199568,"title":"","content":"Edit: Wrong Thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 03-25-2018, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}